    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nbase16\n\n### Description\n\nI realised whilst writing that this is more so an issue with treesitter linking the `@variable` capture to `Identifier` rather than an issue with this plugin itself, but I'd like to post it anyway so you're aware :)\r\n\r\nThe pictures and videos from module demos (for example, [`mini.doc`](/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/6402c79d73c07ad19374dc7b4f9d4bdfc2f57f42/readmes/mini-doc.md#demo)) indicate that variables should be linked to a yellow highlight group (such as `Normal`), but instead are linked to `Identifier` (an orange colour).\r\n\r\nHowever, reading the documentation for [`mini.base16`](/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/6402c79d73c07ad19374dc7b4f9d4bdfc2f57f42/lua/mini/base16.lua#L235) seems to indicate that, for variables, the orange colour (`base08`) is correct.\r\n\r\nI believe the former should be the case (see actual vs expected behaviour below), but maybe I'm wrong on this.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Copy the following code block into `test.lua` (from the `mini.doc` demo):\r\n```lua\r\nlocal MiniDoc = {}\r\n\r\nMiniDoc.config = {\r\n  annotation_extractor = function(l)\r\n    return string.find(l, '^%-%-%-(%S*) ?')\r\n  end,\r\n}\r\n```\r\n2. Look at the highlight group of the variables `string` and `l` inside of the local function body, along with `MiniDoc`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe highlight group of `string` and `l` inside the local function body, along with `MiniDoc` are linked to a yellow highlight group (such as `Normal`). The fields `config`, `annotation_extractor`, along with the parameter `l` inside the local function declaration are linked to `Identifier` (an orange colour).\r\n\r\nThis can be achieved with the command `hi! link @variable Normal`:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/25364469/206426246-d4832cfc-7e05-4128-afd9-bf8cbe3f3103.png)\r\n\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe highlight group of `string` and `l` inside the local function body, along with `MiniDoc` are (incorrectly?) linked to `Identifier` (an orange colour). The fields `config`, `annotation_extractor`, along with the parameter `l` inside the local function declaration are correctly linked to `Identifier`:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/25364469/206425651-ce9414fe-92d5-4671-9089-c7d00fd660dc.png)",
