            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nYes, you are right that using `base08` color is reserved for variables as per [base16 styling guide](https://github.com/chriskempson/base16/blob/main/styling.md).\r\n\r\nYes, I see this as more of a tree-sitter issue. They seem to have changed default linking for variable to `Identifier` when they switched from `TSVariable` to `@variable` highlight group. Interestingly enough, I didn't even notice this :)\r\n\r\nAt the moment, tree-sitter in 'mini.base16' is supported only via defining built-in highlight groups to which tree-sitter groups are linked. Besides decreased complexity, this approach also allowed to avoid breaking during tree-sitter highlight group migration. And the extra problem is that `@variable` highlight group is not supported in Neovim<0.8, so this will introduce branching in code.\r\n\r\nAlthough doable, `hi! link @variable Normal` won't work universally, unfortunately, because it will also add the `guibg` color which will override other background color (like from cursor line).\r\n\r\nAt the moment, I am inclined to let the user fine-tune tree-sitter highlight groups by manually defining them. But I'll think about this more.",
